F. Other changes to the text
<small>
Section 3.2 now contains the divergence proposition (A1), the damped norm, the weight lemma, and the boundedness theorem (A3), together with a remark recording that Lemmas 4 and 5 are not needed for the $m = 1$ bound.
Section 4 now contains a proof of the $q = 1$ dilation stability corollary (A4), which was previously stated without one.
Conclusion: the opening sentence now records the $q = 1$ situation, namely that for $m \ge 2$ the scale measure must be damped, since the input to each layer past the first is nonnegative with positive integral and the undamped norm is infinite. The closing paragraph of the arXiv version, on whether Lipschitz continuity holds for general diffeomorphisms when $q = 1$, has been removed.
Acknowledgments: now record the use of Claude Opus 5 in correcting the $q = 1$ proofs for the undamped norm, which were originally stated as true on the basis of a false proof. The authors checked the output and take responsibility for all results.
</small>.'
